      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "📌 What is the Sigmoid Function?",
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 18,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "📌 What is the Sigmoid Function?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.3636363636363635
    },
    {
      "id": "CMsNghti62KRHWwIMHQVa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -14850,
      "y": -17570,
      "width": 711.5894775390625,
      "height": 90,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2d3436",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "vFDglZB8iOW2_peXRgBCX",
      "index": "bEd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1460880239,
      "version": 240,
      "versionNonce": 1417460623,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785862359021,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Mathematical function that maps any real-valued number to a value between 0 and 1.\n• Characteristic \"S\"-shaped curve, also called the logistic function.\n• Widely used in binary classification to convert outputs to probabilities.\n• Introduces non-linearity into neural networks.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 15,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• Mathematical function that maps any real-valued number to a value between 0 and 1.\n• Characteristic \"S\"-shaped curve, also called the logistic function.\n• Widely used in binary classification to convert outputs to probabilities.\n• Introduces non-linearity into neural networks.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
